  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1215 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nMore great fall weather is in store for the rest of the week! \nUpper level ridging will remain over the central U.S. with some\namplification mid to late week leading to above normal \ntemperatures and dry conditions. As the heights aloft increase\nand 1000-500 hPa thickness expands, expect temperatures to \ngain a few degrees each day. Friday and Saturday look to be the\nwarmest days with widespread mid/upper 70s and the potential \nfor some areas to hit 80 degrees, as h85 temperature anomalies \npeak at +4 to +6C. \n\nDry conditions are expected in conjunction with this warming \ntrend, which brings some concern for fire weather potential. \nHowever, there are two factors at play that should help limit \nthe potential: a gradual increase in low-level moisture and a \nbroad pressure gradient inducing weak surface winds. As such, \nwhile the threat appears low at this time, this remains an area \nto watch as we progress through the week.\n\nHeading through next weekend, a pattern change appears possible\nas a midlevel trough plows into the ridge. This may be our next\nchance for measurable precipitation, though a sizable amount of\ndry air to overcome along with timing/strength/track differences\nwith the ejecting trough keeps confidence low at this time.",
